<robot xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro" name="cell_b">

  <!-- Anchor the cell furniture to the world.

       Every link below is joined by a fixed joint, so converting this URDF to
       SDF lumps the whole cell into ONE link. Without this the simulator gets a
       single free rigid body of a few hundred kilograms resting on the ground
       plane by contact friction alone: joint reaction torques from the arms
       standing on it slide it, and the symptom is base drift that reads as a
       calibration fault and gets debugged in the wrong layer.

       `static` rather than a fixed joint to a link named `world`: nothing here
       has a joint that moves, and a `world` link would also become a second TF
       parent for every body — `robot_state_publisher` would publish it
       alongside the generated static transform table, giving one frame two
       parents. Static costs the physics engine nothing and changes no name. -->
  <gazebo>
    <static>true</static>
  </gazebo>

